Two sealed constraints materially shape the implementation: the loader accepts exactly the five production arms at `learner.py:1169–1171`, and accepts only positive completed epochs ≤2,000 that are divisible by 100 at `:1182–1189`. Therefore the CLI cadence must fail closed unless it is 100 (the checkpoint payload itself also seals 100), and a genuine 2-epoch model checkpoint cannot be read by that loader. I’ll keep this invariant honest: the 2-epoch smoke will exercise training and the gate, while checkpoint write/read verification will use the first admissible 100-epoch synthetic fixture boundary and be reported separately—not forge a 2-epoch cursor. The current generated view corpus also has C1/C2 rows only (`include_coalition=False` in its builder), so no complete five-arm corpus slice exists yet; real-mode ingestion will reject it until an authenticated C3 coalition view is present.
